   "text": "I read this as a DBCO\u2013PEG4\u2013Val\u2013Cit\u2013PAB linker attached to an N\u2011alkoxy tubulysin\u2011type payload. I assembled the SMILES region by region.\n\n**Regions, left to right**\n- **DBCO end:** a dibenzoazacyclooctyne, N\u2011acylated with a succinyl chain (N\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)NH\u2013).\n- **PEG4 spacer:** NH\u2013CH2CH2 followed by four ether oxygens, each separated by CH2CH2, ending in CH2CH2C(=O)\u2013.\n- **Val\u2013Cit\u2013PAB:** L\u2011valine, then L\u2011citrulline (side chain CH2CH2CH2NHC(=O)NH2), then a p\u2011aminobenzyl carbamate (the PAB unit).\n- **Tup unit:** a 4\u2011amino\u20112,2\u2011dimethyl\u20115\u2011arylpentanoic acid, with the aryl ring bearing the carbamate NH.\n- **Thiazole:** a thiazole\u20114\u2011carboxamide whose C2 carries a CH(OAc) group.\n- **Tuv unit:** the CH2 and CH(iPr) that follow, with the nitrogen carrying an O\u2013CH2CH2CH2C\u2261CH (pentynyloxy) group.\n- **Ile\u2013Mep end:** an isoleucine acylated by an N\u2011methyl pipecolic acid.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Tup C4, the acetoxy carbon and the Tuv carbon bearing the iPr group were assigned from the drawn wedges. The Tuv wedge direction was ambiguous and I took it as pointing to the CH2.\n- Val, Cit and Ile were taken as the natural L configuration.\n- The N\u2011methyl pipecolic acid was taken as R, as in natural tubulysin.\n- For these last four centres the wedge/hash marks were not clear enough in the image, so they rest on the natural configuration rather than the drawing.\n\nSMILES: O=C(CCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=O)C(=O)Nc1ccc(COC(=O)Nc2ccc(C[C@@H](CC(C)(C)C(=O)O)NC(=O)c3csc(n3)[C@H](OC(C)=O)C[C@@H](C(C)C)N(OCCCC#C)C(=O)[C@H]([C@@H](C)CC)NC(=O)[C@H]3CCCCN3C)cc2)cc1)N1Cc2ccccc2C#Cc2ccccc21"
